---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_423",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 423,
  "text": " [[1797.16]] <b>346₁.  Ex Cordemoii tractatu de corporis et mentis distinctione\n[[1798.1]] <tit2><b>Ex Cordemoii tractatu <i>De Corporis et mentis distinctione</b></tit2>\n[[1798.2]] [Disc. I] </p>\n<p> [[1798.3]] Ex eo quod natura atque distinctio corporis et materiae non satis clare noscuntur,\n[[1798.4]] fere omnes vulgaris physicae errores oriuntur. </p>\n<p> [[1798.5]] Corpus est substantia extensa, et proinde (cum multa talia sint) limitata seu figura\n[[1798.6]] praedita; et cum unumquodque corpus sit unica eademque substantia, ideo nec dividi nec\n[[1798.7]] ejus figura mutari potest, neque penetrari. <b>Materia</b> est multorum corporum compages;\n[[1798.8]] si plura corpora considerentur ut inter se unita dicentur <b>portio materiae</b>, si unio absit\n[[1798.9]] <b>cumulus</b>, si inter se invicem fluunt <b>liquor</b>, si [partes] connexae inter se, quasi uncinis\n[[1798.10]] quibusdam, vel parvo adeo motu ut facile separari non possint, <b>massa</b>. Corpus partes\n[[1798.11]] habere nequit, sed materia. <b>Clarissima interim substantiae extensae [idea]\n[[1798.12]] est</i>, sed male cum materiae perceptionibus confunditur, non omne extensum divisibile\n[[1798.13]] est. Res considerandae non ut apparent, sed ut sunt, nulla in materia extensio est, nisi quia\n[[1798.14]] unumquodque corpus ex [quo] constat, ea praeditum est, et massa ideo est divisibilis quia\n[[1798.15]] componitur ex partibus quae sunt diversae substantiae. (+ Notabile est tum Cartesianos\n[[1798.16]] vulgares, qui omne extensum divisibile vocant, tum Cordemoium semi Gassendistam qui\n[[1798.17]] omnem substantiam indivisibilem judicat, et vere unam, ad ideas provocare. Forsan ambo\n[[1798.18]] recte ex mea sententia, si enim omnia corpora organica sunt animata et omnia corpora vel\n[[1798.19]] organica vel organicorum corporum collectanea sunt, consequens est, omnem quidem\n[[1798.20]] molem divisibilem esse, sed substantiam ipsam nec dividi nec extingui posse. +) Absque\n[[1798.21]] his physicae principia nosci non possunt. </p>\n<p> [[1798.22]] Magna est consuetudo materiam cum corporibus (+ substantiis extensis +) confundendi.\n[[1798.23]] Verum est corpus esse substantiam extensam, sed falsum est materiam esse\n[[1798.24]] substantiam. Nam unaquaeque substantia in semet ipsam dividi non potest (+ vir clarissimus\n[[1798.25]] confuse et per nebulam vidit veritatem, accurate demonstrare non potuit +) et si\n[[1798.26]] ejus natura in extensione sita est statim ac extensa concipitur, cum eadem in omnibus suis\n[[1798.27]] extremitatibus sit, nullam ejus extremitatem ab alia separabilem esse fatendum est.\n[[1799.1]] (+ Eodem argumento probaret nec corpus humanum posse dividi, quia anima una eademque\n[[1799.2]] in toto corpore existit. Scilicet in eo lapsus est, quod non agnovit, aliud in corporea\n[[1799.3]] substantia dari praeter extensionem a quo scilicet ipsa substantiae notio oriatur, quam\n[[1799.4]] sola extensio dare non potest. Id vero est potentia seu virtus agendi patiendique, secundum\n[[1799.5]] axioma receptissimum quod actiones sunt suppositorum. +) In nullum incidere\n[[1799.6]] potui, quem de materia et corpore tanquam de una eademque re verba facientem audivi,\n[[1799.7]] qui super hac re mentem suam mihi explicare potuerit, etiam quando cum ipsis supponere\n[[1799.8]] volui substantiam esse divisibilem quod menti naturali repugnat. Cum quaesivi an substantia\n[[1799.9]] esset divisibilis in infinitum, negabant, et indefinite divisibilem dicebant, sed hanc\n[[1799.10]] indefinitam divisibilitatem eodem modo explicabant, ut infinitam, et cum tandem candide\n[[1799.11]] faterentur esse in ea re quae captum hominum superent, necesse tamen ajebant, ut res se\n[[1799.12]] ita haberet. In nostra autem sententia eadem obscuritas esse non videtur. Alterum in\n[[1799.13]] contraria opinione incommodum est, quod corporis separati non concepto motu conceptum\n[[1799.14]] formare non possunt, nec secundum eorum doctrinam concipi possit corpus quiescens\n[[1799.15]] inter alia corpora, nam si ab aliis tangitur, eo ipso in unum idemque corpus cum\n[[1799.16]] ipsis conflatur (+ nisi contactus sit in puncto. Sunt quae ipsum Cordemoium premant,\n[[1799.17]] ponamus duas atomos triangulares se tangere et componere quadratum perfectum, et ita\n[[1799.18]] juxta se quiescere, detur alia substantia corporea seu Atomus quadrata aequalis composito\n[[1799.19]] ex his duabus, quaero in quo differant haec duo extensa; certe nulla in ipsis ut nunc\n[[1799.20]] sunt concipi potest diversitas nisi ponamus aliquid in corporibus praeter extensionem, sed\n[[1799.21]] sola memoria pristinorum discernuntur qualis in corporibus nulla est, quomodo diversa in\n[[1799.22]] ipsis deinde evenire possunt, si et tertio aliquo impellantur, ut unum dissiliat in partes,\n[[1799.23]] aliud secus. Hoc premit omnes Atomistas, et cogit fateri dari in materia aliquid aliud ab\n[[1799.24]] extensione. +). Interim habemus perfectam ideam corporis inter alia corpora quiescentis.\n[[1799.25]] (+ Imaginem habemus, fingamus corpus creare substantiam extensam de cujus natura sit\n[[1799.26]] moveri, eadem erunt phaenomena quae nunc et tamen nos fingere poterimus eam quiescere,\n[[1799.27]] prorsus haec imaginatio est, qualis dicentium se concipere vacuum. +) Tertium\n[[1799.28]] incommodum est, quod hinc sequetur, nullum concipi posse momentum quo corpus\n[[1799.29]] eandem magnitudinem et figuram conservare possit, cum scilicet corpus a variis corporibus\n[[1799.30]] ex diversis partibus pellitur, dividetur enim tot modis quot pelletur, et partes\n[[1799.31]] separatae adversus eas quae supersunt repulsae eas ita divident, ut nullus divisionis limes\n[[1799.32]] concipi possit. Et si corpus quadratum circa proprium centrum moveri supponatur et licet\n[[1800.1]] dicant tot partes uniri rursus quot pereant, facile est redire incommodum, ut idem corpus\n[[1800.2]] non permaneat. Coguntur ipsi inter philosophandum supponere multa per aliquod tempus\n[[1800.3]] actualiter non dividi. (+ Imo nil tale coguntur asserere. +) Natura autem ferimur ad\n[[1800.4]] corpus indivisibile concipiendum et corpus ipsum nostrum ex innumeris compositum, ut\n[[1800.5]] unum concipimus, quia omnes partes ita ad finem unum concurrunt ut dividi nequeant,\n[[1800.6]] nisi violata oeconomia, et Jurisconsulti corpus vocant, quicquid sine interitu dividi nequit\n[[1800.7]] (+ imo vocant non corpora, sed species +), quantitatem vero rerum congeriem quae a se\n[[1800.8]] invicem independenter subsistunt, ut triticum vinum oleum. Scilicet naturali idea corpus\n[[1800.9]] rem indivisibilem materia divisibilem repraesentat. Corpus autem non ideo divisibile est,\n[[1800.10]] quia de una extremitate missis aliis cogitare possumus, sed necesse est corpus eo ipso\n[[1800.11]] quia extensum est plures extremitates habere; et potius inde concludes esse inseparabiles,\n[[1800.12]] quia ejusdem sunt extremitates. Ut autem Extensio competit corpori, ita quantitas\n[[1800.13]] materiae. (+ Quidni detur et quantitas extensionis. +) </p>\n<p> [[1800.14]] Non est necesse omnia intervalla esse corporibus plena. Non assentior illis qui\n[[1800.15]] putant sublato contento vasis latera uniri, neque enim intelligo quid unum corpus ad\n[[1800.16]] alterius subsistentiam conferat. (+ Imo omnes substantiae sibi sunt correquisitae. Distantia\n[[1800.17]] non erit substantiae, sed situs. Necesse est situm seu relationem in aliquo fundari, si\n[[1800.18]] dicis in possibili interpositione, dico debere hanc possibilem rursus fundari in aliquo jam\n[[1800.19]] tum actuali. +) </p>\n",
  "number": "346₁.",
  "title": "Ex Cordemoii tractatu de corporis et mentis distinctione",
  "date": null
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:346₁. Ex Cordemoii tractatu de corporis et mentis distinctione Ex Cordemoii tractatu De Corporis et mentis distinctione [Disc. I] Ex eo quod natura atque distinctio corporis et materiae non satis clare noscuntur, fere omnes vulgaris physicae errores oriuntur. Corpus est substantia extensa, et proind...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>